In the evening, I reach my flat.
I video call my younger sister, Sofia.
She is at home in Mexico.
"Chechi, how was the café work?" Sofia asks.
"It was a very good day, Sofia," I say.
I tell her about my first shift.
"I learned to make coffee today."
Sofia laughs and asks, "Did you make mistakes, Chechi?"
"Yes, I have made some mistakes today," I reply.
"But I learned to do new things from those mistakes."
"It was very busy in the café in the morning."
"My first customer was a friendly man."
"He ordered a cappuccino from me."
Sofia claps.
"Then what else did you do?" she asks.
"I also learned to take the customers' orders."
"It was a good experience."
"I have decided to go there next Saturday too for my second shift," I say.
